    "body": "No CI job runs `ctime_tests` on ARM64. The Cirrus \"ARM64: Linux (Debian stable), Valgrind\" task did. #1689 moved it into `valgrind_debian`, whose job-wide `CTIMETESTS: 'no'` turned it off. This sets `CTIMETESTS: 'yes'` on the two arm64 entries.\n\nI ran `ci/ci.sh` for both entries on aarch64 (Debian trixie, Valgrind 3.24, clang 19). Both pass. Both fail under Valgrind after I replace `secp256k1_scalar_cond_negate` in `secp256k1_ecdsa_sig_sign` with `if (high) negate`. Logs on request.\n",
